<!-- purpose: one-page growth experiment spec — falsifiable hypothesis, guardrails, ICE, sample size, flag assignment, instrumentation playback, stop date and SRM gate, write-up -->
<!-- consumes: baseline rate and eligible daily traffic, event catalogue, ICE criteria, flag platform configuration -->
<!-- produces: artefact conforming to content/02-output-contract.xml -->
<!-- depends-on: content/01-core-rules.xml + content/06-decision-tree.xml -->
<!-- token-budget-impact: ~700 tokens when loaded -->
# Growth Experiment {{ experiment_id }} — {{ product_name }}

## Hypothesis
If we <change> for <segment>, then {{ metric_name }} will change by at least <minimum_effect_pct> percent because <mechanism>.

- change: <one change>
- segment: <one segment>
- primary_metric: {{ metric_name }} (a measured rate, never "engagement")
- minimum_effect_pct: <number above 0>
- mechanism: <the belief this test can prove wrong>

## Guardrails (at least three, one per category; a breach vetoes a ship)

| name | category | stop_threshold |
|---|---|---|
| <metric> | revenue_or_conversion | <threshold versus control> |
| <metric> | retention | <threshold versus control> |
| <metric> | performance_or_error | <threshold> |

## ICE (integers 1-10, scored before build against the written criteria)
- impact: <1-10>
- confidence: <1-10; at most 3 unless confidence_evidence cites a prior test, research or analytics>
- ease: <1-10>
- criteria_ref: <path to the team's ICE criteria>
- confidence_evidence: <citation, or null>
- backlog_rank: <position; deviations from ICE order are logged>

## Sample size (alpha 0.05, power 0.8)
- baseline_rate: <rate over the last four closed weeks>
- minimum_detectable_effect_pct: <same as the hypothesis>
- required_per_variant: <from the power calculation>
- eligible_daily_traffic: <users/day in the segment>
- duration_weeks: <ceil(required_per_variant / (eligible_daily_traffic x smallest allocation) / 7), 1 to 8; above 8 redesign>

## Assignment (randomised_controlled, by the flag platform)
- platform: <launchdarkly | statsig | unleash | growthbook | optimizely | internal>
- hash_key: <user_id | account_id>
- control_variant: <variant receiving the unchanged experience>

| variant | percent |
|---|---|
| control | <n> |
| <variant> | <n> (percentages sum to 100) |

## Instrumentation
- exposure_event: <event fired when the user sees the variant> (exposure_logged_at: variant_seen)
- analytics_destination: <where events land>
- metric_events: <primary and guardrail events>
- playback: cohort <staging | one_percent>, performed_on <YYYY-MM-DD>, events_verified <exposure and every metric event, each with experiment id and variant id>; no ramp above the smoke-test allocation until passed

## Schedule and SRM gate
- launch_date: {{ start_date }}
- stop_date: {{ end_date }} (at least duration_weeks whole weeks after launch; results are read only then)
- sequential_method: <null, or the method declared up front>
- srm_check: chi_square_p <observed versus planned allocation>; below 0.001 invalidates the run

## Write-up (within seven days of stop_date, whatever the outcome)
- date: <YYYY-MM-DD>
- log_entry: <shared experiment log reference>
- decision: <ship | iterate | kill; never ship on a breached guardrail or a failed SRM check>
- primary_effect: observed <x> percent, CI <low> to <high>
- guardrail_results: <one line per guardrail with observed value and breached yes/no>
- srm_p: <same as srm_check>
- belief_changed: <one sentence on what the team now believes differently>
- counts_toward_velocity: <true only once this write-up exists>
